Active Constraint Sensitivities to Independent Variables
========================================================
This report lists the affect of moving each independent, while keeping all 
other independent variables constant, on the active constraints.  For each 
independent variable, only movement in the direction of maximizing the objective
is considered.  This is not necessarily the same direction as the variable
was pushed in the solution, since an independent variable may move opposite
to the objective function gradient due to trade-offs with other independent 
variables.  In this report dW/dZ is the derivative of a dependent
variable with respect to an independent variable.

1.  A decrease in the independent variable 
  114 /S6:Equil:PFrac["Liq"]
with objective function gradient value  -8.807E+00
will cause the following active dependent variable bounds to become violated:
                                                                                                                                                             Kuhn-Tucker    dW/dZ
                                                                                                                                                             -----------  ----------
Lower /CURefrigerant:OffsetFromMaxRate                                                                                                                        -6.150E-01   3.228E+01
Upper /S6:Liq:SumMoleFrac                                                                                                                                      6.356E-01  -1.737E+01

2.  A decrease in the independent variable 
  878 /AirFlowControl/MO1:Setpoint
with objective function gradient value  -5.889E-06
will cause the following active dependent variable bounds to become violated:
                                                                                                                                                             Kuhn-Tucker    dW/dZ
                                                                                                                                                             -----------  ----------
Lower /CURefrigerant:OffsetFromMaxRate                                                                                                                        -6.150E-01   5.157E-04

3.  A decrease in the independent variable 
 1015 /RefrigSystem/CT1/MO1:Setpoint
with objective function gradient value  -6.556E-02
will cause the following active dependent variable bounds to become violated:
                                                                                                                                                             Kuhn-Tucker    dW/dZ
                                                                                                                                                             -----------  ----------
Lower /CURefrigerant:OffsetFromMaxRate                                                                                                                        -6.150E-01   1.001E-01
